context_info = ()
for d in context:
    prompt = "Here is a document:\nBEGIN_DOCUMENT\n" + d + "\nEND_DOCUMENT\nTask: Determine if this document mentions or describes a musical act (an individual) that matches any of the following clues. For any candidate(s) with at least one match, output a compact report for that candidate with fields and brief quotes from the document for evidence. If the document is not relevant, output nothing.\nClues to check:\n- Wrote their first original song by age 17.\n- Has a song whose title exactly matches the name of a play written in the late 1500s (e.g., Shakespeare/Marlowe: Romeo and Juliet, A Midsummer Night's Dream, The Merchant of Venice, Much Ado About Nothing, As You Like It, The Two Gentlemen of Verona, Henry IV, etc.).\n- Sold only about 300 copies of their debut single in the 1970s.\n- Worked in the music department for a video game released in 2011 (name the game if mentioned).\n- Married, in the 1970s, a spouse who is a music producer, arranger, and keyboard player (name the spouse if mentioned).\n- That spouse was an uncredited cast member in a 1983 film in which the musician appears in a picture (identify the film if mentioned).\n- Released their first number-one album in 1976 (specify album and chart/country if mentioned).\nFor each candidate that matches any clue, provide:\n- Candidate: [stage/performing name]\n- Birth name: [if in doc]\n- Spouse info: [name, occupation, marriage year]\n- Early songwriting evidence: [quote]\n- Debut single + sales: [quote]\n- Song matching late-1500s play: [song title, play name, quote]\n- 2011 video game music dept: [game title, quote]\n- 1983 film/uncredited spouse + appears-in-picture: [film title, quote]\n- First #1 album in 1976: [album, chart, quote]\nOnly include candidates with at least one of the above supported by the document, and keep each report concise with minimal but sufficient quotes."
    result = llm_query(prompt)
    context_info = context_info + (result,)

aggregated = ""
for r in context_info:
    aggregated = aggregated + r + "\n\n"

final_prompt = "We need to identify a single musical act (an individual performer) whose birth name is being asked. The correct person must satisfy ALL of the following:\n- Wrote their first original song by age 17.\n- Has a song whose title exactly matches the name of a play written in the late 1500s (e.g., Shakespeare/Marlowe titles such as Romeo and Juliet, A Midsummer Night's Dream, Much Ado About Nothing, The Merchant of Venice, As You Like It, The Two Gentlemen of Verona, Henry IV, etc.).\n- Sold only about 300 copies of their debut single in the 1970s.\n- Worked in the music department for a video game released in 2011.\n- Married, in the 1970s, a spouse who is a music producer, arranger, and keyboard player.\n- That spouse was an uncredited cast member in a 1983 film in which the musician appears in a picture.\n- Released their first number-one album in 1976.\n\nHere are extractions from the context documents:\n" + aggregated + "\nBased only on the information above, select the single best-matching candidate who satisfies all of the listed points and provide their birth name. If more than one candidate appears, choose the one that fully satisfies all conditions. Output only the birth name, with no additional text."
result = llm_query(final_prompt)
return_result(result)